      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Feigin, what do you think Congress intended in 1986?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "After a few fits and starts, there were briefs we filed that urged a circumstance-specific approach."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But -- but, Mr. Feigin, you're pointing to a statute where there was something else in addition to the language that's in this provision. And that's -- it was true in Nijhawan and it was true in Hayes, and what the Court pointed to was the something else in addition, the committed by specified persons or the fraud involving over $10,000, and saying that that peculiar -- you know, that that particular language made it clear that somebody had to look to what had"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Well, Your Honor, if you're with me -- if that is the question you're now raising, then we've gotten past offense that is a felony. Then we're all agreed that offense that is a felony could have a categorical approach --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: No, no, no. So I'm interested in the practical implications of our decision in this case. How many contemporaneous crime statutes would be put in jeopardy if we rule in -- if we affirm here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But, just to be clear, do we have any -- we have this very impressionistic argument, you tell us the end of the world is near, or maybe now, after the Chief Justice, it's not quite so close as we thought, and then your friend's going to argue, well, it's not going to really change much at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: -- is there -- is there some absolute -- you know, is there some killing argument against it, which there may well be, which should tell me I'm really either alone or out of my mind or et cetera."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what the Court writes -- I'm not saying we should -- is, in clause A, it is -- it's an offense that is a felony, has an element, the use, attempted use, or threatened use to physical force, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Wait, let me follow up for a second, because the words are \"substantial risk,\" okay? Substantial risk of physical force."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. I just have, I think, four points."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "10bb9263bfa5b37e906cc075e877a2873bf06e3e39fc9b50f67df6737e50676c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-10bb9263bfa5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- the reason that you seem to be touting this reading is that it's going to expand -- has to be -- over the categorical approach the number of defendants that this statute now will apply to."
    },
    {
